# =================================================================================================
# Agent's Player to Club Model -- .gitignore
#
# Written against this project's actual structure (not a generic template). The deployed Streamlit
# app (dashboard/app.py) reads exactly 4 CSVs from production/recommendation_engine/results/ -- see
# dashboard/app_config.py / dashboard/data_loader.py. Everything else under production/ is either
# build-time source (.py scripts, kept -- they document/reproduce the pipeline) or generated
# research/intermediate data (excluded below -- large, not needed at runtime, regenerable from the
# source scripts).
# =================================================================================================

# --- Local backup, never part of the project ---
.pre_gcs_v4_backup/

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- Virtual environments ---
venv/
.venv/
env/

# --- IDE / OS ---
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Secrets / local env (defensive -- none currently exist in this project) ---
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json

# --- Logs / temp ---
*.log
*.tmp

# --- Legacy / superseded work ---
Archive/

# --- Research, experiments, intermediate/build outputs (regenerable from production/*/*.py) ---
# `**/results/` (not just `production/*/results/`) because at least one stage
# (club_pattern_model/system_compatibility_candidate/results/) has a results/ directory nested
# deeper than one level -- caught the hard way: first push included it, see commit history.
production/**/research/
production/**/results/
!production/recommendation_engine/results/
!production/recommendation_engine/results/**

# NOTE: the two negations above re-include production/recommendation_engine/results/ -- it holds
# the 4 CSVs the deployed dashboard reads at runtime (players.csv, recommendations.csv,
# explanations.csv, league_coverage.csv) plus a small (~1KB) build-time stats file. Both negation
# lines are required (the directory itself, then its contents) or git won't descend into it. Do
# not narrow the blanket `production/**/results/` rule without keeping this exception, or the
# deployed app's own data goes missing from the repo.
